research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-13561-QUOTE Throughout, $\mathbb{R}$ is the complete ordered field ([[def-complete-ordered-field]], [[def-ordered-field]]) with its order ([[def-real-order]]). Let $A \subseteq \mathbb{R}$ and let $f : A \to \mathbb{R}$. Then $f$ is:
