research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-1348064-+{"id":"fs-zero-second-derivative-decides-extremum","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_taylor.html","https://www-users.cse.umn.edu/~voronov/5615-20/pdfs/12-2-1.pdf"],"rationale":"The literature states that a zero second derivative is inconclusive and gives the higher-derivative test that distinguishes the three outcomes. The item combines the standard witnesses x^4, -x^4, and x^3 into one explicit refutation.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-1348065-+{"id":"ex-piecewise-polynomial-periodic-oscillator","statement":"ai-generated","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"trivial","urls":[],"rationale":"The normalized quartic Hermite cell 16u^2(1-u)^2, its periodic gluing, and the chosen derivative values are a bespoke local construction. Direct polynomial differentiation gives matching value and first derivative at every seam, periodicity and boundedness are immediate from the fractional-part definition, and substituting the displayed quarter-points gives derivative values 3 and -3.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-1348066-+{"id":"ex-differentiable-function-with-discontinuous-derivative","statement":"ai-generated","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"trivial","urls":[],"rationale":"The witness x^2 psi(1/x) uses the preceding bespoke polynomial oscillator rather than the classical trigonometric example. The difference quotient at zero is bounded by |x| times a fixed bound for psi, while the product/chain calculation and the oscillator's recurring derivative values directly show discontinuity of F' at zero.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-1348067-+{"id":"ex-xk-abs-x-smoothness-threshold","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":[],"rationale":"The family x^k|x| being C^k but not C^{k+1} is a standard elementary smoothness example, and the item's piecewise derivative computation verifies it. A real literature search found the k=2 instance in MIT 18.100B notes but no allowed source stating the full quantified family, so this row requires Alpha's independent established-knowledge concurrence and is not downgraded to invented merely for lack of a full source.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
