research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-1362426-+{"id":"cor-taylor-remainder-bound","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://myweb.uiowa.edu/pbreheny/7110/wiki/taylor-series.html"],"rationale":"The source states the standard Lagrange error estimate M|x-a|^{n+1}/(n+1)! under the same derivative bound. The repository's proof is a direct local application of its preceding remainder theorem.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-1362427-+{"id":"thm-second-derivative-test","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_taylor.html"],"rationale":"The source gives the same pointwise second-derivative test: f'(c)=0 with positive or negative f''(c) yields a strict local minimum or maximum. The item proves it through derivative monotonicity under the same weak pointwise hypothesis.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-1362428-+{"id":"thm-first-nonzero-derivative-test","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www-users.cse.umn.edu/~voronov/5615-20/pdfs/12-2-1.pdf"],"rationale":"The source gives the higher-derivative test with the parity and sign alternatives. The item replaces a neighbourhood C^n hypothesis by the sharper Peano-at-the-point hypothesis and spells out the odd case's increase-through-the-point conclusion.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
