research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-1376754-+{"id":"ex-differentiable-function-with-discontinuous-derivative","statement":"ai-generated","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"trivial","urls":[],"rationale":"The witness x^2 psi(1/x) uses the preceding bespoke polynomial oscillator rather than the classical trigonometric example. The difference quotient at zero is bounded by |x| times a fixed bound for psi, while the product/chain calculation and the oscillator's recurring derivative values directly show discontinuity of F' at zero.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
